//? Title: Maximal scoring subsequences: actual candidate integration and honest predecessor work
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find positive-scoring contiguous intervals that strictly improve on their proper
subintervals and are not contained in longer such intervals. A scored sequence
can contain several disjoint positive signal islands. Native candidate histories
now expose the actual integrations of the original nine scores. The report
separates the Ruzzo-Tompa maximality idea from the direct predecessor scan used
by this implementation.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Let P_j=sum_{i<j} x_i. An interval [a,b) has score P_b-P_a. A strictly maximal
scoring interval improves on each proper subinterval and is not contained in a
longer interval with that property. Strictness excludes zero-score extensions.
Each positive score seeds a candidate with endpoint prefixes L,R. The native
list searches backward for the rightmost prior candidate with smaller L, then
merges that candidate and every following list entry only when its R is also
smaller. Final survivors give the positive maximal intervals. The original paper
has a linear-time linked algorithm. This implementation uses a direct backward
scan and can make
$$ 0+1+\cdots+(m-1)=m(m-1)/2 $$
\alttext(Alternating plus one and minus one scores force the actual direct predecessor scan to make a triangular number of comparisons.)
predecessor tests on m positive seeds separated by -1. The report measures that
actual quadratic path instead of repeating the old linear-time claim.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ruzzo_tompa_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = a::ruzzo_tompa_trace({3, -2, 5});
    std::print("| actual input event | prefix before | prefix after | seeded | comparisons | absorbed | " "candidate count |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.input_index,
                   s.prefix_before, s.prefix_after, s.seeded, s.comparisons,
                   s.absorbed, s.candidates.size());
    g::Diagram d(48, 1100);
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual positive seeds {}", t.positive_seeds));
    d.node("n1", {5, 0},
           std::format("Actual absorbed candidates {}", t.absorbed));
    d.node("n2", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual final score {}", t.segments[0].score));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/ruzzo_tompa_tiny.svg");
}
```
